C7  - 117190
DO  - 10.1016/j.memsci.2019.117190
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85068259404?origin=resultslist
AB  - The high flexibility of microgel synthesis provides a tremendous playground to tune properties of microgels, resulting in a broad variety of gels with tailor-made functionalities. Functionalized on membranes, microgels offer direct tuning of filtration properties of microgel-membrane composites. Regarding microgels as soft model colloids, the investigation of microgel-membrane interaction gives insight into the early formation of fouling layers and their stability. While it is known though that microgel properties strongly depend on the support, only few studies analyzed the behavior of microgels on porous surfaces as needed for membrane applications. In this study poly-(N-isopropylacrylamide) (PNIPAM) based microgels serve as soft model colloids. By successively increasing the concentration of the comonomer acrylic acid (AAc) we tune the charge of the microgels in neutral environment. We systematically study the transversal movement of the differently charged gels adsorbed on a porous polyethersulfone (PES) membrane as a function of convective flow and coating conditions. A 3D-printed online screening module allows us to observe single microgel movement under flow induced shear forces. The microgels exhibit a charge dependent mobility on the porous surface. We use the gained fundamental knowledge of microgel adsorption to achieve 65% retention of a charged dye on PNIPAM-co-AAc modified ultrafiltration and microfiltration membranes while neutral solutes pass. © 2019
