AB  - A novel, versatile approach for the production of ultralow-k polymer films is presented. Depending on the glass-transition temperature of the aromatic polyimide mechanically and thermally stable films are formed that has porosities of ca. 40% and k or ε-values below 1.8. Molecular orientation of the parent polymers allows one to manipulate the foam morphology from spherical to layered structures, which yield the lowest k-values realizable.
