UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/0035204750?origin=resultslist
AB  - A study on thin film polymer foaming technique for low and ultra low-K dielectrics was performed. In thin film polymer foaming technique, the polymer/gas mixture was quenched into a supersaturated state by reducing the pressure and increasing the temperature. It was found that the nucleation and growth of gas cells dispersed throughout the polymer sample evolved rendering films with a microcellular structure. The dielectric constant can be reduced systematically by adjusting the foam morphology with respect to porosity and cell size.
